WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.375 --> 00:00:03.559
Unit eighteen. Hot Things Can Burn!

2
00:00:04.509 --> 00:00:08.236
Hello, everyone! I'm Nurse Bopha, your school nurse.

3
00:00:08.286 --> 00:00:11.905
Hi, Nurse Bopha! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:11.955 --> 00:00:15.891
Today we learn about Hot Things Can Burn. Let's go!

5
00:00:16.577 --> 00:00:19.744
Hot. Say it with me. Hot!

6
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:26.840
Stove. Say it with me. Stove!

7
00:00:30.364 --> 00:00:33.664
Fire. Say it with me. Fire!

8
00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:40.627
Burn. Say it with me. Burn!

9
00:00:44.127 --> 00:00:47.361
Kettle. Say it with me. Kettle!

10
00:00:50.859 --> 00:00:54.392
Careful. Say it with me. Careful!

11
00:00:57.888 --> 00:01:01.705
Cool water. Say it with me. Cool water!

12
00:01:05.209 --> 00:01:08.509
Adult. Say it with me. Adult!

13
00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:21.552
A stove, a fire, and a kettle can be very hot. I stay away from hot things so I do not get a burn. If I get a small burn, an adult cools it with cool water.

14
00:01:21.602 --> 00:01:22.845
I can do that too!

15
00:01:24.178 --> 00:01:29.194
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:29.244 --> 00:01:30.394
Fire!

17
00:01:31.321 --> 00:01:36.579
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:37.779
Cool water!

19
00:01:38.833 --> 00:01:45.567
Did you know? Cool running water is the best first thing to put on a small burn — not ice or toothpaste!

20
00:01:45.617 --> 00:01:47.560
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:48.258 --> 00:01:56.336
Think and answer. What hot things in your home should you stay away from?

22
00:01:56.386 --> 00:01:57.536
Great answer!

23
00:01:58.702 --> 00:02:03.579
Great job today! Stay healthy, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:03.629 --> 00:02:06.274
Goodbye, everyone! Stay healthy!

